# ---- PHI / raw data: NEVER commit ----
# THE SESSION DATA LIVES AT `phi/`, INSIDE THIS WORKSPACE AND OUTSIDE GIT.
#
# It was at `~/phi/PSYCH-ASR/` and it was moved in here on 14 September 2026,
# deliberately, so that a project's data sits with the project. What keeps it
# out of a public repository is this rule and the audit in
# `board/test/tracked.py`, which fails the suite if any of it is ever tracked.
#
# THE DIRECTORY KEPT ITS NAME ON PURPOSE. `ai-config/policy/phi.py` fences any
# path containing `phi/`, whole, by the directory rather than by what is under
# it -- so moving the data did not change a single pattern and the fence cannot
# have silently stopped matching. Renaming this directory to anything else
# would break that, quietly, and the hook would go on looking guarded.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, because that is this file's own hard-won
# lesson: an unanchored `artifacts/` once swallowed the `psych_asr/artifacts/`
# subpackage and `git add -A` reported nothing to do.
/phi/

# Therapy session recordings are identifiable PHI. Filenames themselves
# contain participant IDs. Audio, converted audio, and every transcript or
# diarization artifact derived from them stays out of git.
*.m4a
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
*.mp4
*.mov
data/
transcripts/
diarization/
*.rttm
*.srt
*.vtt

# Transcript/feature outputs (may contain session content)
*.json
*.jsonl
*.csv
*.parquet

# ---- Environments / caches / artifacts ----
venvs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
logs/
slurm_jobs/**/logs/
# ANCHORED TO THE REPO ROOT with a leading slash, all four of them. Unanchored,
# `artifacts/` matches at ANY depth -- and it silently swallowed the whole
# psych_asr/artifacts/ subpackage, which `git add -A` then reported as nothing to
# do. A source directory disappearing from a commit because an output directory
# shares its name is exactly the failure a leading slash prevents.
/scratch/
/artifacts/
/figures/

# ---- Editor / OS / secrets ----
.claude/
.vscode/
.env
.DS_Store

# live tutoring board (Tutor-Board) — scratch space, never tracked
live/

# the board's own config must survive the blanket *.json rule above
!tutorboard.json

# so must the markdown linter's, which is config and not data
!.markdownlint.json

# ---- LaTeX build artifacts ----
# docs/*.tex is the source and docs/*.pdf is the deliverable; everything
# pdflatex writes alongside them regenerates on the next build.
*.aux
*.log
*.nav
*.out
*.snm
*.toc
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
